First, add the following dependencies to your `Cargo.toml` file:
```toml
[dependencies]
elevenlabs = "0.1.0"
tts = "0.1.0"
clipboard = "0.1.0"
```
Then, create a new Rust file (e.g. `main.rs`) and add the following code:
```rust
use elevenlabs::ElevenLabs;
use tts::TTS;
use clipboard::Clipboard;

fn main() {
    // Initialize the ElevenLabs API client
    let api_key = "YOUR_API_KEY_HERE";
    let client = ElevenLabs::new(api_key);

    // Initialize the TTS engine
    let tts = TTS::new();

    // Initialize the clipboard
    let clipboard = Clipboard::new();

    // Get the contents of the clipboard
    let clipboard_text = clipboard.get_text().unwrap();

    // Use the ElevenLabs API to generate a speech synthesis audio file
    let audio_file = client.generate_speech_synthesis(clipboard_text).unwrap();

    // Play the audio file using the TTS engine
    tts.play_audio_file(audio_file).unwrap();
}
```
Make sure to replace `YOUR_API_KEY_HERE` with your actual ElevenLabs API key.

This code initializes the ElevenLabs API client, TTS engine, and clipboard, and then uses the ElevenLabs API to generate a speech synthesis audio file from the contents of the clipboard. Finally, it plays the audio file using the TTS engine.

Note that this is just a simple example, and you may want to add error handling and other features to your app.

